# The API image needs three things from this repository. Everything else is
# upload time and nothing else — `target/` alone is tens of gigabytes, and the
# build context is sent to the daemon (or to Fly's remote builder) in full
# before the first instruction runs.
#
# Deny-all-then-allow rather than a list of exclusions, so a directory added
# next year does not silently join the upload.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates

# Build output that lives *inside* an allowed directory has to be named again.
crates/**/target
# wasm-pack's output. The image builds no front end, and this is 3.5 MB of
# artefact that the server has no use for.
crates/*/pkg
